    "perplexity": {
      "description": "The Holy Bible Live captures Manic Street Preachers performing their landmark 1994 album in full at London’s Roundhouse during the band’s sold-out 20th-anniversary tour in December 2014. The performance preserves all thirteen tracks, from the abrasive “Yes” and politically charged “Ifwhiteamericatoldthetruthforonedayit'sworldwouldfallapart” to the stark “4st 7lb,” “The Intense Humming of Evil,” and “P.C.P.” Musically, the set channels the original record’s tense fusion of alternative rock, post-punk severity, industrial textures, and confrontational lyricism into a forceful live presentation.\n\nIssued by Columbia in expanded formats, the release functions both as a concert document and as a retrospective celebration of The Holy Bible’s enduring influence. Deluxe editions add Kieran Evans’s concert film Be Pure, Be Vigilant, Behave and a new Steven Wilson spatial-audio mix of the original 1994 album, giving the project significance beyond a conventional live album. The result is a compelling record of the Manics revisiting one of British rock’s most uncompromising and critically revered albums with renewed intensity.",
